\image(figures/gn_bridge.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Edge labels are conventional unordered-pair betweenness, not distances or raw native source sums. The table retains both scales; the original triangles and bridge are produced by a reusable native graph generator.)
\alttext(Two native triangles joined at vertices 2 and 3 show conventional bridge score nine, four adjacent scores four and the two remaining scores one. A table prints the actual raw values, including bridge eighteen.)

For a simple unweighted undirected graph, let σst be the number of shortest paths
from s to t, and σst(e) the number using edge e. Disconnected pairs contribute zero:

$$
B(e)=\sum_{s<t,\;\sigma_{st}>0}\frac{\sigma_{st}(e)}{\sigma_{st}},
\qquad R(e)=2B(e).
$$
\alttext(Conventional undirected betweenness sums each connected unordered pair’s fraction of shortest paths using the edge. The native source-summed raw value is twice that.)

Equal shortest paths share a pair’s unit weight; they are not each counted as a
whole independent pair. [Girvan and Newman’s original paper](https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.122653799)
removes a highest-betweenness edge and recalculates after removal. Here the preserved
native variant removes every edge within an absolute 10^-12 of the maximum RAW
score in one batch, then recalculates. It may therefore follow a different hierarchy
and return more communities than requested. All edges and paths are unweighted.

> Follow the two equal routes through a diamond

In the diamond 0–1–3 and 0–2–3, source 0 has two shortest paths to vertex 3.
Each predecessor receives a contribution of 1/2 from that endpoint. After those
contributions, vertices 1 and 2 each pass 1+1/2 back to the source. The records
below come from the actual executing BFS and reverse accumulation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gn_diamond.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/girvan_newman.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/network_data.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1},{0,2},{1,3},{2,3}};const auto t=dm::algorithms::edge_betweenness_trace(4,edges);using K=dm::algorithms::GirvanNewmanEventKind;
 std::print("| source-0 popped vertex | actual distance | actual shortest-path count |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.events)if(e.kind==K::pop&&e.source==0)std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} |\n",e.u,e.distance,e.paths_u);
 std::print("\n| predecessor u | successor v | paths to u | paths to v | successor dependency before | actual contribution |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");std::vector<double> contribution(edges.size());
 for(const auto&e:t.events)if(e.kind==K::dependency&&e.source==0){std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.1f} | {:.1f} |\n",e.u,e.v,e.paths_u,e.paths_v,e.dependency_v,e.contribution);contribution[e.index]=e.contribution;}
 std::print("\nActual source initializations {}; path updates {}; dependency updates {}; conservative integer-count guarantee {}.\n",t.result.work.source_initializations,t.result.work.path_updates,t.result.work.dependency_updates,t.result.path_counts_integer_guaranteed);
 const std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint,4> pos{{{0,0},{3,1.7},{3,-1.7},{6,0}}};dm::graphics::Diagram d(80,1000);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle node;node.circle=true;node.width=.8;node.height=.8;node.padding=9;node.font_size=22;
 for(std::size_t u=0;u<4;++u)d.node(std::to_string(u),pos[u],std::to_string(u),node);
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.result.edges.size();++i)d.link(std::to_string(t.result.edges[i].first),std::to_string(t.result.edges[i].second),std::format("{:.1f}",contribution[i]));
 d.text({3,3.2},"Actual source-0 contributions, not all-source scores",23).text({3,-3.1},"Two routes to vertex 3 split its unit weight equally",23).save_svg("build/gn_diamond.svg");
 if(contribution[0]!=1.5||contribution[2]!=.5)throw std::runtime_error("equal-route fractions");
}
