Cycle raw score per edge 4.0; conventional 2.0; native keep test uses raw score < maximum - 1e-12.
\image(figures/gn_batch.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The cycle’s four equal raw scores are all removed in one batch. This deliberately preserves the existing near-maximum policy; it is not a demonstration of single-edge recomputation or an exactly-k partitioner.)
\alttext(A cycle of four labelled vertices is shown before deletion and as four isolated vertices afterward. The table preserves the original bridge result and the zero-scoring early stop for already disconnected pairs.)

The exact native keep condition is R(e)<max R−10^-12. Thus its half-score scale
would have a 5×10^-13 threshold, not 10^-12. Directions and duplicates are ignored,
self-loops discarded, and the remaining edges sorted before adjacency construction.
Output components follow ascending roots and BFS member order; they are not
promised to have sorted members. The empty graph accepts only target 1, returning
no groups; its default target 2 is invalid. These are API contracts, not evidence
of any particular social grouping.

> A genuine friendship graph, acquired through the native library

[Mark Newman’s original network collection](https://websites.umich.edu/~mejn/netdata/)
provides the friendship topology from [Zachary’s 1977 study](https://doi.org/10.1086/jar.33.4.3629752).
The native accessor verifies the source ZIP, GML and README checksums and maps
original ids 1..34 to native ids 0..33. It returns 34 vertices and 78 undirected,
unweighted edges. The source archive contains no faction labels; colours below
mean algorithm components and are not a claimed comparison with observed factions.
The layout is a separate seeded native drawing, not an input to community detection.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gn_karate.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/girvan_newman.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/network_data.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto data=dm::datasets::karate_club();const auto n=data.node_ids.size();const auto r=dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_run(n,data.edges,2);const auto q=dm::algorithms::graph_modularity(n,data.edges,r.groups);
 std::print("Verified original graph: {} vertices, {} source edges, directed {}; original ids {}..{}; native id = original id - 1.\n",n,data.edges.size(),data.directed,data.node_ids.front(),data.node_ids.back());
 std::print("First at-least-two split: {} groups after {} scored batches and {} removals; original-graph modularity {:.12f}.\n\n| component | vertices | original source ids in actual BFS order |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n",r.groups.size(),r.work.rounds,r.work.removed_edges,q);
 for(std::size_t c=0;c<r.groups.size();++c){std::string ids;for(auto u:r.groups[c])ids+=std::format("{} ",data.node_ids[u]);std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",c,r.groups[c].size(),ids);}
 const auto pos=dm::algorithms::force_directed_layout(n,data.edges,400,7);auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();for(auto [u,v]:data.edges)plot.lines({pos[u].x,pos[v].x},{pos[u].y,pos[v].y},"",{148,163,184},1);
 const std::array<dm::graphics::RGB,2> colours{{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}};for(std::size_t c=0;c<r.groups.size();++c){std::vector<double>x,y;for(auto u:r.groups[c]){x.push_back(pos[u].x);y.push_back(pos[u].y);}plot.points(x,y,std::format("Component {}",c),colours.at(c),7);}
 plot.legend({"Component 0","Component 1"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}}).title("Karate friendship graph: native first split").xlab("Native layout x").ylab("Native layout y").x_limits(-1.15,1.15).y_limits(-1.15,1.15).size(850,850).save_svg("build/gn_karate.svg");
 if(n!=34||data.edges.size()!=78||r.groups.size()!=2||r.work.rounds!=10||r.work.removed_edges!=11)throw std::runtime_error("pinned karate first split");
}
