\caption(All original edges remain visible, including edges removed by the detection algorithm. The native mapping retains original source ids in the table. Layout seed and drawing geometry have no role in the betweenness or modularity calculations.)
\alttext(The complete verified 34-node,78-edge friendship graph is drawn with native force-directed coordinates and coloured by the first two returned components. The actual BFS source-id lists, ten scored batches, eleven removals and original-graph modularity are printed.)

> Score every visited partition against the original graph

A divisive method always produces some partition, including on graphs without a
meaningful community interpretation. Modularity compares internal edges with a
degree-based baseline. For group c, let Lc be its internal ORIGINAL edges and Kc its
sum of ORIGINAL degrees, with m original edges:

$$
Q=\sum_c\left[\frac{L_c}{m}-\left(\frac{K_c}{2m}\right)^2\right].
$$
\alttext(Modularity sums each group’s fraction of original internal edges minus the square of its original degree share. Removed algorithm edges still count in this diagnostic.)

[Newman and Girvan’s modularity definition](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.69.026113)
uses the full original network even after detection removes edges. The native
helper therefore receives the original edge list each time. It validates a complete,
disjoint partition and defines Q=0 for an edgeless graph. Maximizing Q over the
visited batch stages does not prove global optimality or a true community count.
Every actual stage below is retained, including unchanged component counts and
worse late partitions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gn_modularity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/girvan_newman.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/network_data.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto data=dm::datasets::karate_club();const auto n=data.node_ids.size();const auto t=dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(n,data.edges,n,200000);using K=dm::algorithms::GirvanNewmanEventKind;
 std::vector<std::vector<std::size_t>> groups,best_groups;std::vector<double>x,qs,counts;std::size_t active=0;double best=-std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();std::size_t best_round=0;
 std::print("| actual round | active edges before cut | components | original-graph modularity | maximum raw edge score |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.events){if(e.kind==K::round)active=e.count;else if(e.kind==K::components)groups.assign(e.count,{});else if(e.kind==K::vertex)groups.at(e.index).push_back(e.u);else if(e.kind==K::maximum||e.kind==K::stop){const double q=dm::algorithms::graph_modularity(n,data.edges,groups);x.push_back(e.round);qs.push_back(q);counts.push_back(groups.size());if(q>best){best=q;best_round=e.round;best_groups=groups;}if(e.kind==K::maximum)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.12f} | {:.9f} |\n",e.round,active,groups.size(),q,e.maximum);else std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.12f} | no scored cut |\n",e.round,active,groups.size(),q);}}
 std::print("\nMaximum among visited stages: round {}; groups {}; original-graph Q {:.12f}. Complete records {}; scored batches {}; actual removed edges {}.\n",best_round,best_groups.size(),best,t.events.size(),t.run.work.rounds,t.run.work.removed_edges);
 auto qplot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();qplot.lines(x,qs,"Q",{37,99,235},2).points(x,qs,"",{37,99,235},3).title("Original-graph modularity").xlab("Actual batch stage").ylab("Q on original 78 edges").y_limits(-.1,.45);
 auto cplot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();cplot.lines(x,counts,"Components",{220,38,38},2).points(x,counts,"",{220,38,38},3).title("Actual component count").xlab("Actual batch stage").ylab("Components").y_limits(0,38);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(qplot).add(cplot).size(1100,540).title("All actual stages retained; peak Q is only among visited partitions").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gn_modularity.svg");
 if(t.events.size()!=174531||best_round!=21||best_groups.size()!=5||std::abs(best-.4012984878369494)>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("independent karate trajectory");
}
