> Complete online records and whole generated graphs have distinct limits

Primitive traces count fixed-schema canonical edges, round/component metadata,
source initializations, actual BFS/path/dependency operations, score rows and
removal decisions. The positive quota is checked before each whole-record append;
its default is one million, and zero disables only that optional quota. Earlier
local work may occur before a later append rejects. No partial trace returns,
no numerical replay reconstructs it, and no caller input is mutated or truncated.

Input vectors, root/work metadata, final ordinary output, working predecessor/BFS
arrays and queues, and allocator storage are excluded. Complete records are not
numeric entries or bytes; this is not a peak RAM limit. Ordinary/run APIs have no
trace quota. Even empty early-stop calls retain their actual metadata records.
Graph generators separately admit whole vertex counts before allocation; that
quota has different units from history records. Numeric and container guards remain
when optional quotas are zero.

All endpoints are validated before target and history checks. Counts must fit the
legacy int distance range; target is positive and valid for the vertex count.
Modularity requires a complete disjoint partition, including isolated vertices.
The GML reader separately validates original ids, endpoints, syntax and bounded
source/node/edge ingress; the verified dataset accessor does not invent missing data.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gn_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/girvan_newman.hpp>
#include <datamunge/datasets/network_data.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(2,{{0,1}},2,33);bool rejected=false,empty_rejected=false,whole_rejected=false,invalid=false,target=false;
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(2,{{0,1}},2,32);}catch(const std::length_error&){rejected=true;}
 const auto empty=dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(0,{},1,4);try{(void)dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(0,{},1,3);}catch(const std::length_error&){empty_rejected=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::clique_bridge_graph(3,3,1,5);}catch(const std::length_error&){whole_rejected=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(2,{{0,1},{0,99}},1,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
 try{(void)dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(0,{},2,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){target=true;}
 auto copy=t;copy.events[0].count=999;copy.run.groups[0][0]=999;const bool owned=t.events[0].count!=999&&t.run.groups[0][0]!=999;
 const auto graph=dm::algorithms::clique_bridge_graph(3,3,1,6);
 std::print("| admitted resource | complete count | rejected cap | rejection observed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Two-vertex actual trace | {} | 32 | {} |\n| Empty early-stop metadata | {} | 3 | {} |\n| Whole generated vertices | {} | 5 | {} |\n",t.events.size(),rejected,empty.events.size(),empty_rejected,graph.vertex_count,whole_rejected);
 std::print("\nIndependent owned copies {}; invalid final endpoint before history quota {}; empty invalid target before quota {}; zero optional history quota retains {} records.\n",owned,invalid,target,dm::algorithms::girvan_newman_trace(2,{{0,1}},2,0).events.size());
 auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.events.size()),32.},{"Captured","Rejected cap"});a.title("Online primitive history").xlab("").ylab("Complete records, not bytes").y_limits(0,40);
 auto g=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(graph.vertex_count),5.},{"Admitted","Rejected cap"});g.title("Whole graph generation").xlab("").ylab("Vertices").y_limits(0,8);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(g).size(1100,500).title("Primitive-record quotas and generated-vertex quotas have different units").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gn_controls.svg");
 if(!rejected||!empty_rejected||!whole_rejected||!invalid||!target||!owned)throw std::runtime_error("admission and ownership");
}
